      "author_handle": "drclaylowder",
      "author_followers": 99300,
      "caption": "If your stomach’s acting up, here’s the real plan from a medical standpoint:\n\nSkip the “pink stuff” for ongoing symptoms—it may help short term, but it’s not addressing the root of the problem.\nFor nausea, Emetrol is a solid option and often works well without being overly harsh.\nIf you’re dealing with reflux or heartburn, medications like omeprazole or Prevacid actually reduce acid production and give your esophagus time to heal. These work best when taken consistently, not just as needed.\nFor quick, immediate relief, Tums can still be helpful to neutralize acid in the moment.\n\nAlso pay attention to triggers—late meals, caffeine, alcohol, and spicy foods are common culprits. Small changes there can make a big difference.\n\nTreat the cause, not just the symptoms. That’s how you actually start to feel better. #fyp #heart #medical #guthealth #doctor ",
